## Windows platform detection

Note that `deleteIfExists` itself does **not** contain Windows-specific platform detection — it relies solely on the OS-agnostic error codes above. Windows detection occurs elsewhere in the file via `platform.isWindows`. For example, in `_getWindowsRetryDelay`:

```dart
if (!platform.isWindows) {
  return null;
}
```

And in `_onFileSystemException`, which routes to `_handleWindowsException` when `platform.isWindows` is true.

## The file-not-found constant

```dart
/// On Windows this is error code 2: ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND, and on
/// macOS/Linux it is error code 2/ENOENT: No such file or directory.
const int kSystemCodeCannotFindFile = 2;
